spans.s:
Kauṇḍinya,
(1) original name of Ājñāta-k˚, q.v. (so also Pali Koṇḍañña): SP 〔206.10〕; 〔207.7〕 (Kauṇḍinyagotra); Divy 〔480.12〕; Karmav 〔161.17〕; LV 〔419.4〕; 〔421.7〕; he was the first who knew or understood the Buddhaʼs Law, hence his name Ājñāta-k˚, cf. LV 〔421.1—2〕 dharmacakraṃ pravartitaṃ, Kauṇḍinyena ca ājñātaṃ;
(2) n. of a brahman, seemingly not the same as prec. tho the latter was a brahman in origin: Suv 〔12.6 ff.〕; 〔108.3〕; 〔110.1〕;
(3) the family name of Śarabhaṅga, q.v.: Mv 〔iii.370.12〕;
(4) n. of a group of 2000 Buddhas: Mv 〔i.58.10〕;
(5) ˚nya-gotra, having the family name K., said of (Ājñāta-)K. in SP above, and of 300 former Buddhas, each of whom predicted the next following one, except the last who predicted the Buddha Candana: Mv 〔iii.233.8—9, 13 ff.〕; 〔234.5〕.
